# local runtime / secrets — never commit
data/
.env
*.pem
id_swgpush*
CLAUDE.md
# previews & build cruft
dryrun/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# local scratch / notes (never commit)
scratchpad/
tasks.txt
# internal tooling + notes — deliberately NOT published. These lived only in .git/info/exclude, which is
# local to one clone: a fresh clone of this repo did not have them, so a single `git add -A` there would
# have pushed them. The rule belongs with the repo, not with one machine's config.
.campaign/
docs/
# …and how we work ON the product is not part of it. `.claude/settings.local.json` below is ignored
# for a different reason (one machine's config); this one is a shared, deliberate non-shipment.
# ⚠️ NO TRAILING COMMENTS IN THIS FILE — `#` only starts a comment at line start, so a pattern with
# one appended is read as literal text and silently matches nothing. That is how this line's first
# version was written, and `git check-ignore` is what caught it.
.claude/skills/
# ⚠️ `tests/` has no leading slash, so it matches at ANY depth — `nix/tests/` included. A flake
# builds from the GIT TREE, so a VM test written there would reach `nix build` as ABSENT, the
# same way amneziawg.png would have (below). The shipped VM tests live in `nix/checks/`, which
# is also what the flake output is called. Do not create `nix/tests/`.
tests/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json.bak
access_harness.py
# test-harness / screenshot cruft (never commit)
.playwright-mcp/
*.png
# …except the README screenshots (committed, referenced by the README files)
!screenshots/
!screenshots/*.png
# …and except the client logo swg-sub SERVES. It is a shipped asset, not a screenshot: it is in
# SUB_WEB, in the Dockerfile's COPY and in swg-sub's own allow-list. It survives today only because
# it was tracked before the *.png rule existed — `git add -A` in a fresh clone would drop it, and a
# flake builds from the GIT TREE, so the derivation would then fail to evaluate (measured).
!amneziawg.png
